1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:02,000
*music*

2
00:00:30,000 --> 00:00:46,700
Well good morning, love the energy. Hope you all are doing well. If we haven't had the privilege of meeting yet, my name is Ryan and I have the privilege of being one of the pastors here.

3
00:00:46,700 --> 00:00:56,440
I'm so glad that you have joined us as we are in a series on the book of Ephesians. We are taking big chunks intentionally so that we kind of don't lose the force for the trees.

4
00:00:56,440 --> 00:01:02,700
Sometimes you study through a book of the Bible, you can get so fixated on one word or one phrase that you kind of lose sight of the context.

5
00:01:02,700 --> 00:01:11,720
And so we're trying to weave this balance where we keep the context in our minds without just breezing past really big truths.

6
00:01:11,720 --> 00:01:21,100
So we're hopefully weaving that really well. Week one, Kent said that God has chosen and adopted the church to live as the working model of new creation.

7
00:01:21,180 --> 00:01:29,440
That we are intended to both pray, Father in heaven, may your kingdom come and your will be done on earth as it is in heaven.

8
00:01:29,440 --> 00:01:34,580
That's a prayer that God has given us to pray and it is also a prayer that he has given us to participate in.

9
00:01:34,580 --> 00:01:45,320
That the church gets to be the hands and feet of Jesus, modeling to the rest of the world what it would look like for his kingdom to come on earth as it is in heaven.

10
00:01:46,440 --> 00:01:56,680
Week two, we said that the church exists through the power of God, by the blood of Jesus, both redeeming us as sinful individuals and reconciling us into a community.

11
00:01:56,680 --> 00:02:00,180
That is one thing that the gospel does for us.

12
00:02:00,180 --> 00:02:01,660
It is not two separate things.

13
00:02:01,660 --> 00:02:02,960
Those things have to happen.

14
00:02:03,420 --> 00:02:13,020
And the American evangelical church is often so fixated on individuals being saved from their sin that we haven't really gotten the reconciled to one another part very good.

15
00:02:13,020 --> 00:02:22,680
And we have to hold those two things together that we have been redeemed to God and reconciled to one another in a new family with a new primary identity.

16
00:02:23,680 --> 00:02:42,020
And then last week we said, weirdly enough, that it is from the foundation of the earth that God had planned to demonstrate his wisdom, his manifold wisdom to the powers and principalities through the church, through the way that we live.

17
00:02:42,100 --> 00:02:47,700
And Aaron, if you can throw up that graphic, I think this is any, are we have any office fans in the room?

18
00:02:47,700 --> 00:02:49,120
A couple?

19
00:02:49,120 --> 00:02:49,820
Yeah, right?

20
00:02:49,820 --> 00:02:51,820
You missed 100% of the shots.

21
00:02:51,820 --> 00:02:53,740
You don't take Wayne Gretzky, Michael Scott.

22
00:02:53,740 --> 00:03:01,720
This is Tim Mackey's chart that we have stolen and April has made our own.

23
00:03:01,720 --> 00:03:05,620
And so this is Tim Mackey, Canvas Community Church.

24
00:03:05,620 --> 00:03:14,680
But I think this really articulates what Paul is doing through chapters one through three, on the far half of the circle.

25
00:03:14,680 --> 00:03:22,840
That from the beginning, when sin entered the world, we have broken up into different categories of people.

26
00:03:22,840 --> 00:03:28,460
And we are at war with one another for what feels like a limited amount of resources.

27
00:03:30,040 --> 00:03:49,980
And we are separated from God and we are under the rule and reign of the powers and principalities who are animating whatever they can animate to get us to turn away from God and to turn away from one another and to steal and to kill and destroy the life and flourishing that God has created and woven into the fabric of creation.

28
00:03:49,980 --> 00:03:56,480
They are destroying it and we are allowing them to do so by actively participating in what they want.

29
00:03:57,280 --> 00:04:03,600
And it's all leading to the cross, the manifold wisdom of God, Jesus' death, burial, resurrection, and ascension.

30
00:04:03,600 --> 00:04:09,700
And for those of us that have placed our faith in Jesus, we have been raised above the powers and principalities of this era.

31
00:04:09,700 --> 00:04:11,000
We have been seated with him.

32
00:04:11,000 --> 00:04:15,640
We have been gathered together, diverse and unified into the local church.

33
00:04:15,640 --> 00:04:20,260
And the church is the new working model of creation.

34
00:04:20,360 --> 00:04:22,800
This is kind of what we've gotten through the first three weeks.

35
00:04:22,800 --> 00:04:24,800
Hopefully that isn't sounding new to you.

36
00:04:24,800 --> 00:04:27,460
If it is, then I did not preach as well as I thought I did.

37
00:04:27,460 --> 00:04:29,760
And Kent did not preach as well as I thought he did.

38
00:04:29,760 --> 00:04:32,200
So that's where we're at.

39
00:04:32,200 --> 00:04:36,240
And now Paul is going to make this shift and he's going to focus in on that central circle.

40
00:04:36,240 --> 00:04:42,460
And he's going to say, what does it look like for the church to be the new working model of creation?

41
00:04:42,460 --> 00:04:47,740
Because we are human, there is a way in which we can place our faith in this cosmic thing that God has done.

42
00:04:47,740 --> 00:04:52,260
We can believe that we have been raised and seated above the powers and principalities.

43
00:04:52,260 --> 00:04:55,380
And yet we can function as if nothing has changed at all.

44
00:04:56,500 --> 00:05:01,840
And so Paul is now going to make this transition to say, all of these things that I have said about you is true.

45
00:05:01,840 --> 00:05:05,220
Now, will you walk in those things?

46
00:05:05,220 --> 00:05:07,340
Will you live in those things?

47
00:05:07,340 --> 00:05:10,340
Because there is a way in which we can believe them and not do them.

48
00:05:10,340 --> 00:05:13,300
And Paul says, that's a problem.

49
00:05:13,300 --> 00:05:15,840
Because that's no longer our identity.

50
00:05:15,840 --> 00:05:18,480
That's just something that we've agreed upon.

51
00:05:18,480 --> 00:05:20,780
Identity has outworking.

52
00:05:20,780 --> 00:05:21,560
Does that make sense?

53
00:05:21,560 --> 00:05:26,180
And Paul roots all of this, this transition in prayer.

54
00:05:26,500 --> 00:05:27,800
Because he knows it's hard.

55
00:05:27,800 --> 00:05:30,320
And he knows that we are prone to wander.

56
00:05:30,320 --> 00:05:35,240
And that we are prone to kind of walk back and forth from the church back to the powers and principalities.

57
00:05:35,240 --> 00:05:39,280
And so I think because Paul roots it in prayer, we should also root it in prayer.

58
00:05:39,280 --> 00:05:44,500
So let's just pray that we would not just understand what is theologically true,

59
00:05:44,500 --> 00:05:48,400
but that our identity would change the way that we live together in community.

60
00:05:48,400 --> 00:05:50,520
Father in heaven, we thank you.

61
00:05:52,040 --> 00:06:00,240
For Ephesians chapter 1 through 3, for this bold declaration of the manifold wisdom of God.

62
00:06:00,240 --> 00:06:07,240
From before the foundations of the earth to save rebellious and broken people

63
00:06:07,240 --> 00:06:10,340
and to redeem us into a right relationship with you

64
00:06:10,340 --> 00:06:13,560
and to reconcile us into a right relationship with one another.

65
00:06:15,600 --> 00:06:22,340
And yet, God, we still feel the tension of the fear and anxiety of not having enough,

66
00:06:22,340 --> 00:06:27,540
of our vision for life feeling lost.

67
00:06:27,540 --> 00:06:29,220
And so we still fight.

68
00:06:29,220 --> 00:06:30,140
We still grasp.

69
00:06:30,140 --> 00:06:35,500
We still look at other people as obstacles to our life and flourishing.

70
00:06:37,580 --> 00:06:38,820
And we need you.

71
00:06:38,820 --> 00:06:43,780
We need the power of the Holy Spirit at work in us to change our mindset,

72
00:06:43,780 --> 00:06:46,860
to get our eyes above the powers and principalities

73
00:06:46,860 --> 00:06:49,540
and on the kingdom of heaven now.

74
00:06:49,540 --> 00:06:53,300
Inaugurated and soon to be consummated.

75
00:06:53,300 --> 00:06:59,980
God, we are desiring participants, but not always willing participants.

76
00:07:01,400 --> 00:07:06,460
And so by the power of your spirit, show us what it looks like for us to live this out.

77
00:07:06,460 --> 00:07:15,260
God, for this local body, may we be a people that not only understand our spiritual identity,

78
00:07:15,260 --> 00:07:18,420
but live into it by your power.

79
00:07:18,420 --> 00:07:23,120
And God, may it change the families that we are raising,

80
00:07:23,120 --> 00:07:25,660
the neighborhoods where we are living,

81
00:07:26,560 --> 00:07:30,460
the communities that we are, find ourselves in.

82
00:07:30,460 --> 00:07:36,180
God, may heaven be more clearly visible in Frederick County

83
00:07:36,180 --> 00:07:39,260
because this group of people understand their identity

84
00:07:39,260 --> 00:07:42,800
and live it out by your power, for your glory,

85
00:07:42,800 --> 00:07:45,180
for our good and for the good of our neighbors.

86
00:07:45,180 --> 00:07:46,580
It's in Jesus' name I pray.

87
00:07:46,580 --> 00:07:47,340
Amen.

88
00:07:47,340 --> 00:07:50,780
We're going to be in Ephesians chapter 4.

89
00:07:50,780 --> 00:07:53,560
I couldn't decide where to stop at,

90
00:07:53,660 --> 00:07:57,520
so we ended up, I think we're going to go through verse 16 today,

91
00:07:57,520 --> 00:08:00,280
and then we're just going to cover a really big section next week.

92
00:08:00,280 --> 00:08:02,200
I just, I was struggling,

93
00:08:02,200 --> 00:08:05,860
and I just decided that this week's problems were going to become next week's problems.

94
00:08:05,860 --> 00:08:10,280
We just don't have enough time before Easter to cover the things that I thought we would be able to cover,

95
00:08:10,280 --> 00:08:14,300
and so I just, I pushed off my problem this week to next week.

96
00:08:14,300 --> 00:08:16,500
So we're going to cover verses 1 through 16.

97
00:08:16,500 --> 00:08:19,220
If you want to follow along with me when we get there,

98
00:08:19,920 --> 00:08:23,380
you guys are hearing lots of dad illustrations recently,

99
00:08:23,380 --> 00:08:24,420
and I'm sorry about that,

100
00:08:24,420 --> 00:08:28,020
but parenting really has taught me a lot about myself,

101
00:08:28,020 --> 00:08:29,740
about God,

102
00:08:29,740 --> 00:08:33,520
and about how much smarter my two-year-old is than I am.

103
00:08:33,520 --> 00:08:35,560
You know the show,

104
00:08:35,560 --> 00:08:37,880
Are You Smarter Than a Fourth Grader?

105
00:08:38,560 --> 00:08:40,900
I am nowhere near ready for that show,

106
00:08:40,900 --> 00:08:42,900
because I am not smarter than my two-year-old.

107
00:08:42,900 --> 00:08:48,360
And one way I discovered this recently is I was picking him up from his daycare,

108
00:08:48,360 --> 00:08:51,000
and we have a long drive home from daycare,

109
00:08:51,000 --> 00:08:52,860
and we just did the potty training thing,

110
00:08:52,860 --> 00:08:54,340
and so I was like,

111
00:08:54,340 --> 00:08:54,520
all right,

112
00:08:54,520 --> 00:08:55,840
I'm going to take you to the bathroom.

113
00:08:55,840 --> 00:08:58,220
So I take him to the bathroom at daycare,

114
00:08:58,220 --> 00:08:59,340
and instinctively,

115
00:08:59,340 --> 00:09:00,820
because he's in the spot,

116
00:09:00,820 --> 00:09:01,880
he's at daycare,

117
00:09:01,880 --> 00:09:03,040
he walks over,

118
00:09:03,040 --> 00:09:03,800
grabs the stool,

119
00:09:03,800 --> 00:09:04,840
slides it up to the urinal,

120
00:09:04,840 --> 00:09:06,300
pulls his pants and his underwear down,

121
00:09:06,300 --> 00:09:07,100
and just starts going.

122
00:09:07,100 --> 00:09:10,460
And I'm dumbfounded,

123
00:09:10,460 --> 00:09:12,860
because I've never seen him do any of those things.

124
00:09:12,860 --> 00:09:14,980
Because at home,

125
00:09:14,980 --> 00:09:16,680
I pull his pants down for him.

126
00:09:16,680 --> 00:09:17,440
At home,

127
00:09:17,440 --> 00:09:18,560
I get the stool ready.

128
00:09:18,560 --> 00:09:18,960
At home,

129
00:09:18,960 --> 00:09:23,720
I do all of this prep work that needs to happen for him to go to the bathroom,

130
00:09:23,720 --> 00:09:25,060
and I'm just like,

131
00:09:25,060 --> 00:09:26,560
all right, dude,

132
00:09:26,560 --> 00:09:30,100
you've been pulling the wool over my eyes here.

133
00:09:30,100 --> 00:09:34,820
I had no clue that you were as capable of doing these things

134
00:09:34,820 --> 00:09:36,780
as you thought you were.

135
00:09:36,780 --> 00:09:38,180
It shocked me,

136
00:09:38,180 --> 00:09:43,200
because he's able to do far more than I ever thought that he could do.

137
00:09:43,200 --> 00:09:45,040
And if I'm honest,

138
00:09:45,040 --> 00:09:47,300
as cool as it was,

139
00:09:47,300 --> 00:09:49,220
as awesome as it was to see this,

140
00:09:49,220 --> 00:09:51,820
this just ingenuity,

141
00:09:51,820 --> 00:09:54,340
this individualism that he just can do on his own,

142
00:09:54,340 --> 00:09:57,060
oftentimes I am happier to do it for him

143
00:09:57,060 --> 00:09:59,140
than to let him do it himself.

144
00:09:59,140 --> 00:10:01,160
Because when I do it,

145
00:10:01,160 --> 00:10:02,300
it's faster,

146
00:10:02,300 --> 00:10:03,900
it's better,

147
00:10:03,900 --> 00:10:05,720
there's less of a mess,

148
00:10:05,720 --> 00:10:06,580
right?

149
00:10:06,580 --> 00:10:09,760
But me doing it for him

150
00:10:09,760 --> 00:10:11,660
is an obstacle to his maturity,

151
00:10:11,660 --> 00:10:14,280
and it is also an obstacle to my maturity.

152
00:10:15,280 --> 00:10:19,740
Because it is the slow process of teaching him to do something for himself

153
00:10:19,740 --> 00:10:22,520
that he is going to need to do for himself

154
00:10:22,520 --> 00:10:26,800
that is hard on my patience and my unsanctified self.

155
00:10:26,800 --> 00:10:30,640
And so there's this process of me training him how to do a thing

156
00:10:30,640 --> 00:10:33,560
that is hard for me and hard for him,

157
00:10:33,560 --> 00:10:36,960
and it actually ends up maturing both of us in the process.

158
00:10:36,960 --> 00:10:39,000
And as I was studying Ephesians chapter 4,

159
00:10:39,000 --> 00:10:41,180
this image came to my mind

160
00:10:41,180 --> 00:10:43,640
because I think it illustrates some primary challenges

161
00:10:43,640 --> 00:10:45,900
that we as the church face

162
00:10:45,900 --> 00:10:48,560
with the exhortations that Paul is going to give us.

163
00:10:48,560 --> 00:10:52,940
See, Paul moves from what God did through Christ

164
00:10:52,940 --> 00:10:54,080
by the power of the Spirit

165
00:10:54,080 --> 00:10:56,820
for individuals bringing us into a right family with God,

166
00:10:56,820 --> 00:10:57,800
new unified family,

167
00:10:57,800 --> 00:11:00,400
and towards our practical responsibilities.

168
00:11:00,400 --> 00:11:03,200
What does it look like for us to live

169
00:11:03,200 --> 00:11:06,480
as redeemed people of this new unified family?

170
00:11:06,480 --> 00:11:11,140
He roots it in this illustration of learning to walk.

171
00:11:11,140 --> 00:11:14,520
Like we mature as we learn to walk

172
00:11:14,520 --> 00:11:17,940
in the direction that God has turned us around, right?

173
00:11:17,940 --> 00:11:20,020
Changed our name, he turned us around.

174
00:11:20,020 --> 00:11:22,120
We are living to walk in this new direction.

175
00:11:22,120 --> 00:11:27,620
But I think if many of us are honest with ourselves,

176
00:11:27,620 --> 00:11:33,020
we are content more to be passive participants than active.

177
00:11:33,200 --> 00:11:36,420
We are like Rory, willing to let somebody else

178
00:11:36,420 --> 00:11:38,540
do the work of the kingdom for us.

179
00:11:38,540 --> 00:11:42,460
We'd rather sit back and complain about the health

180
00:11:42,460 --> 00:11:43,800
and maturity of a church

181
00:11:43,800 --> 00:11:46,880
than actually be an active participant

182
00:11:46,880 --> 00:11:49,480
in helping mature the church.

183
00:11:50,480 --> 00:11:53,300
Or we come to receive gifts from the church

184
00:11:53,300 --> 00:11:56,840
without contributing gifts that we have been given.

185
00:11:56,840 --> 00:12:00,440
And there are many leaders in the church,

186
00:12:00,440 --> 00:12:01,580
myself included,

187
00:12:01,580 --> 00:12:06,080
who find it much easier to just do the work of the ministry

188
00:12:06,080 --> 00:12:08,320
than to equip the saints to do the work of the ministry,

189
00:12:08,320 --> 00:12:11,200
which Paul is going to tell us later in Ephesians.

190
00:12:12,300 --> 00:12:15,140
And I think ultimately what we need to learn here

191
00:12:15,140 --> 00:12:18,220
is that if we want to mature as a body of believers,

192
00:12:18,220 --> 00:12:20,760
we all have to be participating in the role

193
00:12:20,760 --> 00:12:24,480
that God has placed us, placed on our lives.

194
00:12:24,480 --> 00:12:30,240
Being a passive participant is not an option.

195
00:12:30,240 --> 00:12:33,580
And leaders just doing the work for the people

196
00:12:33,580 --> 00:12:34,540
is not an option.

197
00:12:34,540 --> 00:12:36,740
The kingdom of God requires all of us

198
00:12:36,740 --> 00:12:38,060
to be active participants.

199
00:12:38,060 --> 00:12:40,820
And this is slow, hard,

200
00:12:40,820 --> 00:12:43,780
and like taking Rory to the bathroom,

201
00:12:43,780 --> 00:12:45,180
a messy process.

202
00:12:45,180 --> 00:12:49,560
But it will lead to our maturity.

203
00:12:49,560 --> 00:12:55,080
Paul is going to challenge this inclination

204
00:12:55,080 --> 00:12:57,560
by saying every one of us has been saved by grace,

205
00:12:57,560 --> 00:12:59,080
brought into the family of God.

206
00:12:59,080 --> 00:13:02,080
And we are called to walk in unity with diversity

207
00:13:02,080 --> 00:13:03,780
and towards maturity

208
00:13:03,780 --> 00:13:06,000
so that we can be an effective working model

209
00:13:06,000 --> 00:13:07,860
of new creation on earth.

210
00:13:07,860 --> 00:13:10,720
Many pastors and theologians,

211
00:13:10,720 --> 00:13:12,060
we've talked about this a little bit before,

212
00:13:12,060 --> 00:13:13,260
many pastors and theologians

213
00:13:13,260 --> 00:13:15,780
kind of separate chapters one through three

214
00:13:15,780 --> 00:13:16,640
and four through six

215
00:13:16,640 --> 00:13:19,580
into like theology and practice

216
00:13:19,580 --> 00:13:21,060
or doctrine and duty

217
00:13:21,060 --> 00:13:22,920
is a phrase that I've seen

218
00:13:22,920 --> 00:13:24,140
because for whatever reason,

219
00:13:24,140 --> 00:13:25,340
theologians and pastors feel like

220
00:13:25,340 --> 00:13:26,240
they have to use words

221
00:13:26,240 --> 00:13:27,260
that start with the same letter

222
00:13:27,260 --> 00:13:28,200
or it doesn't count.

223
00:13:28,200 --> 00:13:29,600
It's not spiritual

224
00:13:29,600 --> 00:13:30,980
if you don't use words

225
00:13:30,980 --> 00:13:31,980
that start with the same letter.

226
00:13:31,980 --> 00:13:34,520
So we got this doctrine and duty.

227
00:13:34,660 --> 00:13:35,920
But what I want us to realize

228
00:13:35,920 --> 00:13:37,740
is it's not doctrine and duty,

229
00:13:37,740 --> 00:13:39,380
but it's identity and vocation.

230
00:13:39,380 --> 00:13:41,420
That Ephesians chapter four

231
00:13:41,420 --> 00:13:42,420
is going to make this shift

232
00:13:42,420 --> 00:13:43,440
of what does it look like

233
00:13:43,440 --> 00:13:44,580
for the church to live out

234
00:13:44,580 --> 00:13:46,540
the vocation of the church.

235
00:13:46,540 --> 00:13:48,880
And if you have notes

236
00:13:48,880 --> 00:13:50,300
or if you have your bulletin,

237
00:13:50,300 --> 00:13:51,360
I do have notes on the back.

238
00:13:51,360 --> 00:13:52,980
The first point I want to see here

239
00:13:52,980 --> 00:13:54,300
is that Paul says that

240
00:13:54,300 --> 00:13:56,220
in order for us to live into our vocation,

241
00:13:56,220 --> 00:13:58,740
we have to first walk in unity.

242
00:13:59,840 --> 00:14:01,880
No, Paul has not moved on from unity.

243
00:14:01,880 --> 00:14:04,020
Yes, we start at unity in chapter two.

244
00:14:04,020 --> 00:14:06,100
And the first thing he says

245
00:14:06,100 --> 00:14:07,420
is what it looks like for us

246
00:14:07,420 --> 00:14:09,560
to live out this working model

247
00:14:09,560 --> 00:14:10,180
of new creation

248
00:14:10,180 --> 00:14:12,240
is that we have to stay committed

249
00:14:12,240 --> 00:14:13,420
to walking in unity.

250
00:14:13,420 --> 00:14:15,100
Ephesians chapter four, verse one.

251
00:14:15,100 --> 00:14:17,600
As a prisoner for the Lord,

252
00:14:17,600 --> 00:14:20,340
then again, humble brag by Paul.

253
00:14:20,340 --> 00:14:21,180
He's reminding you

254
00:14:21,180 --> 00:14:22,380
that he's in jail for the gospel.

255
00:14:23,380 --> 00:14:25,680
I urge you to live a life

256
00:14:25,680 --> 00:14:27,020
worthy of the calling

257
00:14:27,020 --> 00:14:28,000
which you have received.

258
00:14:28,000 --> 00:14:29,820
Be completely humble and gentle.

259
00:14:29,820 --> 00:14:30,580
Be patient,

260
00:14:30,580 --> 00:14:33,420
bearing with one another in love.

261
00:14:33,420 --> 00:14:35,960
Make every effort

262
00:14:35,960 --> 00:14:38,420
to keep the unity of the spirit

263
00:14:38,420 --> 00:14:40,400
through the bond of peace.

264
00:14:40,400 --> 00:14:42,440
In Romans, he would say it this way.

265
00:14:42,440 --> 00:14:42,860
He'd say,

266
00:14:42,860 --> 00:14:46,320
as much as is possible,

267
00:14:46,320 --> 00:14:48,720
live at peace with one another.

268
00:14:48,720 --> 00:14:52,180
There is one body and one spirit,

269
00:14:52,280 --> 00:14:54,000
just as you were called to one hope

270
00:14:54,000 --> 00:14:55,240
when you were called one Lord,

271
00:14:55,240 --> 00:14:56,940
one faith, one baptism,

272
00:14:56,940 --> 00:14:59,100
one God and father of all

273
00:14:59,100 --> 00:15:00,640
who is over all

274
00:15:00,640 --> 00:15:03,560
and through all and in all.

275
00:15:03,560 --> 00:15:04,800
Last week, I asked you

276
00:15:04,800 --> 00:15:06,980
to look for a theme word,

277
00:15:06,980 --> 00:15:08,280
a central word in the text.

278
00:15:08,280 --> 00:15:09,280
Can anybody shout out

279
00:15:09,280 --> 00:15:10,020
what the main word

280
00:15:10,020 --> 00:15:11,260
in the text is this morning?

281
00:15:11,260 --> 00:15:13,080
One, right?

282
00:15:13,080 --> 00:15:15,020
There's this unity concept

283
00:15:15,020 --> 00:15:17,500
built into what Paul is saying here.

284
00:15:17,500 --> 00:15:19,700
From the very beginning

285
00:15:19,700 --> 00:15:20,860
of the vocation of the church,

286
00:15:20,860 --> 00:15:22,220
what matters is that we live

287
00:15:22,220 --> 00:15:23,280
in right relationship

288
00:15:23,280 --> 00:15:24,840
with one another.

289
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:28,360
And he uses this really strong term.

290
00:15:28,360 --> 00:15:30,020
My translation says urge.

291
00:15:30,020 --> 00:15:32,800
I urge you to live a life

292
00:15:32,800 --> 00:15:34,020
worthy of your calling,

293
00:15:34,020 --> 00:15:35,540
to live into the vocation

294
00:15:35,540 --> 00:15:37,660
that you have been adopted into

295
00:15:37,660 --> 00:15:38,820
in the church.

296
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:40,800
And urge is an extremely strong word

297
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:41,240
in the Greek

298
00:15:41,240 --> 00:15:42,960
that doesn't translate well,

299
00:15:42,960 --> 00:15:43,900
or at least that's what people

300
00:15:43,900 --> 00:15:44,940
who know Greek way better

301
00:15:44,940 --> 00:15:46,000
than I do tell me.

302
00:15:46,000 --> 00:15:47,660
I feel like sometimes

303
00:15:47,660 --> 00:15:48,960
I say these phrases to you

304
00:15:48,960 --> 00:15:50,220
and you think that they're for me.

305
00:15:51,220 --> 00:15:52,320
When I say the word

306
00:15:52,320 --> 00:15:53,280
doesn't translate well,

307
00:15:53,280 --> 00:15:54,680
somebody else has told me that,

308
00:15:54,680 --> 00:15:54,980
okay?

309
00:15:54,980 --> 00:15:57,500
Like my Greek is down here.

310
00:15:57,500 --> 00:15:58,240
All right.

311
00:15:58,240 --> 00:15:59,640
But they tell me

312
00:15:59,640 --> 00:16:00,880
that it doesn't translate well.

313
00:16:00,880 --> 00:16:02,640
It's a strong phrase

314
00:16:02,640 --> 00:16:04,520
and I love how Carl Barth

315
00:16:04,520 --> 00:16:05,300
summarized it.

316
00:16:05,300 --> 00:16:06,780
Carl Barth says

317
00:16:06,780 --> 00:16:07,720
that he,

318
00:16:07,720 --> 00:16:09,140
when he translates this text,

319
00:16:09,140 --> 00:16:10,060
when he paraphrases it

320
00:16:10,060 --> 00:16:11,320
into his terminology,

321
00:16:11,320 --> 00:16:11,860
he says,

322
00:16:11,860 --> 00:16:13,520
yours is the initiative.

323
00:16:13,520 --> 00:16:15,720
Do it now.

324
00:16:15,720 --> 00:16:17,920
It's this strong,

325
00:16:17,920 --> 00:16:18,800
like he's moving.

326
00:16:18,800 --> 00:16:20,460
He's moving from what God

327
00:16:20,460 --> 00:16:22,160
has done for us in Christ

328
00:16:22,160 --> 00:16:23,840
to what is your responsibility

329
00:16:23,840 --> 00:16:25,140
now that you have been brought

330
00:16:25,140 --> 00:16:26,140
into the family of God.

331
00:16:26,140 --> 00:16:27,580
It is a strong transition

332
00:16:27,580 --> 00:16:28,920
from God has chosen,

333
00:16:28,920 --> 00:16:29,840
God has adopted,

334
00:16:29,840 --> 00:16:31,260
God has saved you by grace

335
00:16:31,260 --> 00:16:32,320
apart from works.

336
00:16:32,320 --> 00:16:33,600
But now that he has done that,

337
00:16:33,600 --> 00:16:36,180
you have a participation to do.

338
00:16:36,300 --> 00:16:37,420
And I urge you,

339
00:16:37,420 --> 00:16:40,200
I strongly challenge you

340
00:16:40,200 --> 00:16:41,740
that yours is the initiative

341
00:16:41,740 --> 00:16:43,840
to do it now.

342
00:16:43,840 --> 00:16:47,200
So what is this urgent initiative?

343
00:16:47,200 --> 00:16:49,180
That's so important.

344
00:16:49,180 --> 00:16:49,600
He says,

345
00:16:49,600 --> 00:16:51,300
I urge you,

346
00:16:51,300 --> 00:16:52,880
I strongly challenge you

347
00:16:52,880 --> 00:16:54,740
to walk in a manner

348
00:16:54,740 --> 00:16:56,520
worthy of your calling.

349
00:16:56,520 --> 00:16:58,560
First walk.

350
00:16:58,560 --> 00:17:00,360
He says it's a change of direction

351
00:17:00,360 --> 00:17:01,600
in Ephesians chapter two

352
00:17:01,600 --> 00:17:04,140
and verse two and verse 10.

353
00:17:04,140 --> 00:17:05,460
He uses the same words here.

354
00:17:05,580 --> 00:17:06,340
Ephesians chapter two,

355
00:17:06,340 --> 00:17:06,960
verse two.

356
00:17:06,960 --> 00:17:08,680
I should have highlighted it.

357
00:17:08,680 --> 00:17:09,700
Now I can't find it.

358
00:17:09,700 --> 00:17:11,460
As for you,

359
00:17:11,460 --> 00:17:12,900
you were dead in your transgressions

360
00:17:12,900 --> 00:17:14,860
and sins in which you used to walk

361
00:17:14,860 --> 00:17:16,200
when you followed the ways

362
00:17:16,200 --> 00:17:16,820
of this world.

363
00:17:16,820 --> 00:17:18,620
And then in Ephesians chapter two,

364
00:17:18,620 --> 00:17:19,900
verse 10,

365
00:17:19,900 --> 00:17:20,220
he says,

366
00:17:20,220 --> 00:17:21,440
for we are God's workmanship

367
00:17:21,440 --> 00:17:22,460
created in Christ Jesus

368
00:17:22,460 --> 00:17:23,920
to walk in them.

369
00:17:23,920 --> 00:17:24,920
These are words

370
00:17:24,920 --> 00:17:25,900
that we don't see in the English.

371
00:17:25,900 --> 00:17:26,880
These are the same words.

372
00:17:26,880 --> 00:17:27,860
You used to walk

373
00:17:27,860 --> 00:17:29,100
under the authority

374
00:17:29,100 --> 00:17:30,420
of the powers and principalities.

375
00:17:30,420 --> 00:17:31,280
Now you have been called

376
00:17:31,280 --> 00:17:32,980
to walk with Christ.

377
00:17:32,980 --> 00:17:35,180
And this is a new direction.

378
00:17:35,180 --> 00:17:36,960
It is an urgent thing

379
00:17:36,960 --> 00:17:38,040
that we need to turn around

380
00:17:38,040 --> 00:17:38,920
and walk away

381
00:17:38,920 --> 00:17:39,980
from where we were going

382
00:17:39,980 --> 00:17:40,740
and walk to

383
00:17:40,740 --> 00:17:42,340
where God has called us to.

384
00:17:42,340 --> 00:17:45,220
It is our calling

385
00:17:45,220 --> 00:17:46,800
that we are called to walk in,

386
00:17:46,800 --> 00:17:48,100
which is an eternal hope

387
00:17:48,100 --> 00:17:48,760
of inheritance

388
00:17:48,760 --> 00:17:50,040
rooted in the community

389
00:17:50,040 --> 00:17:51,400
of the church.

390
00:17:51,400 --> 00:17:52,600
Our urgent initiative

391
00:17:52,600 --> 00:17:54,000
is to walk away

392
00:17:54,000 --> 00:17:55,320
from our former way of living

393
00:17:55,320 --> 00:17:57,020
and towards the kingdom of God,

394
00:17:57,020 --> 00:17:59,260
united with one another.

395
00:17:59,860 --> 00:18:01,300
But how do we do that?

396
00:18:01,300 --> 00:18:03,080
Well,

397
00:18:03,080 --> 00:18:05,380
Paul gave us a couple of adjectives

398
00:18:05,380 --> 00:18:06,880
to explain how this happens.

399
00:18:06,880 --> 00:18:08,180
He says,

400
00:18:08,180 --> 00:18:11,120
it's your urgent initiative.

401
00:18:11,120 --> 00:18:11,980
Do it now.

402
00:18:11,980 --> 00:18:12,940
Walk in a manner

403
00:18:12,940 --> 00:18:14,400
worthy of your calling.

404
00:18:14,400 --> 00:18:15,080
How?

405
00:18:15,080 --> 00:18:17,320
By being completely humble,

406
00:18:17,320 --> 00:18:19,080
gentle,

407
00:18:19,080 --> 00:18:20,720
patient,

408
00:18:21,600 --> 00:18:22,660
and enduring

409
00:18:22,660 --> 00:18:23,740
with one another

410
00:18:23,740 --> 00:18:25,140
in love.

411
00:18:25,140 --> 00:18:30,100
I love the stark contrast

412
00:18:30,100 --> 00:18:31,080
between verse one

413
00:18:31,080 --> 00:18:31,760
and verse two.

414
00:18:31,760 --> 00:18:34,820
This is an urgent initiative.

415
00:18:34,820 --> 00:18:37,060
I need you to do it now.

416
00:18:39,060 --> 00:18:40,620
Do it with humility,

417
00:18:40,620 --> 00:18:42,360
patience,

418
00:18:42,360 --> 00:18:45,200
gentleness,

419
00:18:45,200 --> 00:18:46,940
enduring love.

420
00:18:46,940 --> 00:18:47,780
Now,

421
00:18:47,780 --> 00:18:49,100
I haven't had the privilege

422
00:18:49,100 --> 00:18:50,420
or maybe the burden

423
00:18:50,420 --> 00:18:51,620
of spending much time

424
00:18:51,620 --> 00:18:52,540
in the corporate world,

425
00:18:52,540 --> 00:18:53,500
but from conversations

426
00:18:53,500 --> 00:18:54,560
with many of you,

427
00:18:54,560 --> 00:18:55,680
my guess is

428
00:18:55,680 --> 00:18:56,800
that if your workplace

429
00:18:56,800 --> 00:18:58,300
had an urgent initiative

430
00:18:58,300 --> 00:18:59,740
that needed to be done now,

431
00:18:59,740 --> 00:19:00,680
the core values

432
00:19:00,680 --> 00:19:01,640
of that project

433
00:19:01,640 --> 00:19:03,440
would not be humility,

434
00:19:03,440 --> 00:19:05,360
gentleness,

435
00:19:05,360 --> 00:19:06,940
patience,

436
00:19:06,940 --> 00:19:08,540
and enduring love.

437
00:19:08,600 --> 00:19:09,700
Anybody from the corporate world

438
00:19:09,700 --> 00:19:10,720
give me an amen on that?

439
00:19:10,720 --> 00:19:13,700
If you have an urgent initiative

440
00:19:13,700 --> 00:19:14,960
in the secular world,

441
00:19:14,960 --> 00:19:16,260
it is get on board

442
00:19:16,260 --> 00:19:17,040
or get out.

443
00:19:17,040 --> 00:19:18,140
Do the work now.

444
00:19:18,140 --> 00:19:19,520
Suck it up, buttercup, right?

445
00:19:19,520 --> 00:19:21,080
Like, we got stuff to do.

446
00:19:21,080 --> 00:19:22,000
We got to get it done.

447
00:19:22,000 --> 00:19:25,520
And Paul says,

448
00:19:25,520 --> 00:19:26,920
he says,

449
00:19:26,920 --> 00:19:30,820
there is an urgent kingdom initiative

450
00:19:30,820 --> 00:19:32,380
that you have been brought into

451
00:19:32,380 --> 00:19:33,360
as the church,

452
00:19:33,360 --> 00:19:35,940
and you have to do it

453
00:19:35,940 --> 00:19:37,040
at the pace of relationship.

454
00:19:38,140 --> 00:19:39,300
In the kingdom,

455
00:19:39,300 --> 00:19:40,380
we have been given

456
00:19:40,380 --> 00:19:41,560
an urgent initiative,

457
00:19:41,560 --> 00:19:42,440
but it moves

458
00:19:42,440 --> 00:19:43,760
at the pace of relationship,

459
00:19:43,760 --> 00:19:45,680
and it results

460
00:19:45,680 --> 00:19:46,420
in our unity

461
00:19:46,420 --> 00:19:47,520
and maturity.

462
00:19:47,520 --> 00:19:48,880
We all have a part

463
00:19:48,880 --> 00:19:49,900
to play,

464
00:19:49,900 --> 00:19:50,660
but since unity

465
00:19:50,660 --> 00:19:51,140
and maturity

466
00:19:51,140 --> 00:19:51,600
are the goal,

467
00:19:51,600 --> 00:19:52,640
we are called to do it

468
00:19:52,640 --> 00:19:53,340
at the pace

469
00:19:53,340 --> 00:19:54,000
of relationships.

470
00:19:54,000 --> 00:19:55,180
It is God's timing

471
00:19:55,180 --> 00:19:56,060
and not our own.

472
00:19:56,060 --> 00:19:57,460
I think because

473
00:19:57,460 --> 00:19:59,020
we only have a short time

474
00:19:59,020 --> 00:20:00,220
to live on this earth,

475
00:20:00,220 --> 00:20:01,420
we hear urgent initiative,

476
00:20:01,420 --> 00:20:02,080
and we think,

477
00:20:02,180 --> 00:20:03,040
oh, I love the Lord.

478
00:20:03,040 --> 00:20:04,180
I love what he's done for me.

479
00:20:04,180 --> 00:20:05,580
I've got to get stuff done.

480
00:20:05,580 --> 00:20:08,700
And to God,

481
00:20:08,700 --> 00:20:10,680
a thousand years is a day.

482
00:20:10,680 --> 00:20:12,620
A day is a thousand years.

483
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:13,960
He's not worried about pace.

484
00:20:13,960 --> 00:20:16,420
He's worried about humility,

485
00:20:16,420 --> 00:20:17,140
gentleness,

486
00:20:17,140 --> 00:20:18,860
bearing with one another in love.

487
00:20:18,860 --> 00:20:19,980
He's worried about relationships.

488
00:20:19,980 --> 00:20:21,020
He's worried about the image

489
00:20:21,020 --> 00:20:22,820
of Christ being formed in us

490
00:20:22,820 --> 00:20:24,160
and through us

491
00:20:24,160 --> 00:20:26,560
to a watching world.

492
00:20:26,560 --> 00:20:27,840
We've been given

493
00:20:27,840 --> 00:20:28,760
an urgent initiative

494
00:20:28,760 --> 00:20:29,940
and it moves at the pace

495
00:20:29,940 --> 00:20:31,200
of relationship.

496
00:20:31,200 --> 00:20:31,900
But I think much

497
00:20:31,900 --> 00:20:33,040
of the church in America,

498
00:20:33,040 --> 00:20:34,140
if I'm being honest,

499
00:20:34,140 --> 00:20:35,000
and even in the way

500
00:20:35,000 --> 00:20:36,060
that I have participated

501
00:20:36,060 --> 00:20:36,800
in the church

502
00:20:36,800 --> 00:20:37,800
and the way that I have led

503
00:20:37,800 --> 00:20:39,180
and pastored churches

504
00:20:39,180 --> 00:20:40,600
is we are more captured

505
00:20:40,600 --> 00:20:41,960
by the corporate imagination

506
00:20:41,960 --> 00:20:43,560
than a kingdom one.

507
00:20:43,560 --> 00:20:46,420
We often run the church

508
00:20:46,420 --> 00:20:47,280
like a corporation

509
00:20:47,280 --> 00:20:48,500
demanding that members

510
00:20:48,500 --> 00:20:49,120
get on board

511
00:20:49,120 --> 00:20:49,860
with our vision

512
00:20:49,860 --> 00:20:50,500
or get out.

513
00:20:50,500 --> 00:20:52,620
We cater to consumers.

514
00:20:52,820 --> 00:20:54,640
Rather than to maturing believers.

515
00:20:54,640 --> 00:20:57,240
And we run this place

516
00:20:57,240 --> 00:20:58,980
like a corporation.

517
00:20:58,980 --> 00:21:00,560
And Paul says,

518
00:21:00,560 --> 00:21:02,200
yes, there is an urgent initiative,

519
00:21:02,200 --> 00:21:03,600
but that initiative moves

520
00:21:03,600 --> 00:21:05,040
at the pace of relationships.

521
00:21:05,040 --> 00:21:07,380
You cannot force people

522
00:21:07,380 --> 00:21:08,260
to get on board

523
00:21:08,260 --> 00:21:08,940
with your vision.

524
00:21:08,940 --> 00:21:10,340
You have to lead them

525
00:21:10,340 --> 00:21:12,180
and mature them

526
00:21:12,180 --> 00:21:13,960
and invite them in

527
00:21:13,960 --> 00:21:16,560
to this kingdom participation.

528
00:21:16,560 --> 00:21:19,860
Many American Christians,

529
00:21:19,860 --> 00:21:21,500
because we've been discipled

530
00:21:21,500 --> 00:21:22,980
by this American idea,

531
00:21:22,980 --> 00:21:24,660
we're drawn to churches

532
00:21:24,660 --> 00:21:25,560
like this.

533
00:21:25,560 --> 00:21:28,140
Because we've been discipled

534
00:21:28,140 --> 00:21:28,740
by our culture

535
00:21:28,740 --> 00:21:29,740
to believe that things

536
00:21:29,740 --> 00:21:30,840
that are fast-paced,

537
00:21:30,840 --> 00:21:31,740
exciting,

538
00:21:31,740 --> 00:21:32,360
and big

539
00:21:32,360 --> 00:21:33,320
are inherently good.

540
00:21:33,320 --> 00:21:35,220
And I bet

541
00:21:35,220 --> 00:21:36,000
that if you guys

542
00:21:36,000 --> 00:21:37,000
have spent any time

543
00:21:37,000 --> 00:21:38,360
looking up Bible verses

544
00:21:38,360 --> 00:21:39,060
on your phone

545
00:21:39,060 --> 00:21:41,700
that your social media feed

546
00:21:41,700 --> 00:21:44,960
is full of highly published,

547
00:21:44,960 --> 00:21:46,360
highly polished,

548
00:21:46,840 --> 00:21:48,020
massive churches

549
00:21:48,020 --> 00:21:49,960
with podcasts

550
00:21:49,960 --> 00:21:50,740
and platforms

551
00:21:50,740 --> 00:21:51,440
telling you

552
00:21:51,440 --> 00:21:51,960
what it means

553
00:21:51,960 --> 00:21:52,940
to be a good Christian.

554
00:21:52,940 --> 00:21:54,220
Because we have

555
00:21:54,220 --> 00:21:56,000
incentivized churches

556
00:21:56,000 --> 00:21:58,280
looking like the corporate world.

557
00:21:58,280 --> 00:21:59,500
And I'm not saying

558
00:21:59,500 --> 00:22:00,920
that those are necessarily bad,

559
00:22:00,920 --> 00:22:01,500
but I'm saying

560
00:22:01,500 --> 00:22:02,220
the fact that

561
00:22:02,220 --> 00:22:03,000
because he has

562
00:22:03,000 --> 00:22:04,600
a nice backdrop

563
00:22:04,600 --> 00:22:06,460
on his podcast,

564
00:22:06,460 --> 00:22:07,680
or she has a nice backdrop

565
00:22:07,680 --> 00:22:08,440
on her podcast,

566
00:22:08,440 --> 00:22:09,900
she's got a good lighting rig

567
00:22:09,900 --> 00:22:11,260
and her audio

568
00:22:11,260 --> 00:22:12,120
is produced well,

569
00:22:12,120 --> 00:22:12,780
that that means

570
00:22:12,780 --> 00:22:14,640
that she's doing kingdom work.

571
00:22:15,240 --> 00:22:16,460
That's an American assumption.

572
00:22:16,460 --> 00:22:18,800
We think because things

573
00:22:18,800 --> 00:22:19,760
move fast,

574
00:22:19,760 --> 00:22:20,960
are exciting,

575
00:22:20,960 --> 00:22:21,640
and big,

576
00:22:21,640 --> 00:22:22,940
they're inherently good.

577
00:22:22,940 --> 00:22:24,560
When oftentimes

578
00:22:24,560 --> 00:22:26,260
the kingdom is small,

579
00:22:26,260 --> 00:22:27,300
slow,

580
00:22:27,300 --> 00:22:28,520
and ordinary.

581
00:22:28,520 --> 00:22:30,940
Think back to Corey's sermon

582
00:22:30,940 --> 00:22:32,220
on the parable

583
00:22:32,220 --> 00:22:33,200
of the mustard seed.

584
00:22:33,200 --> 00:22:34,740
Kingdom is like

585
00:22:34,740 --> 00:22:36,320
the smallest seed.

586
00:22:36,320 --> 00:22:39,260
It grows slowly,

587
00:22:39,260 --> 00:22:40,080
but over time

588
00:22:40,080 --> 00:22:41,220
it consumes everything.

589
00:22:41,220 --> 00:22:43,440
And I think in America,

590
00:22:43,440 --> 00:22:44,940
the way that we often run

591
00:22:44,940 --> 00:22:45,360
our churches

592
00:22:45,360 --> 00:22:47,000
is we want things to,

593
00:22:47,000 --> 00:22:47,580
we want it to be

594
00:22:47,580 --> 00:22:48,320
the biggest seed

595
00:22:48,320 --> 00:22:49,280
that grows the fastest.

596
00:22:49,280 --> 00:22:52,460
And there's a lot

597
00:22:52,460 --> 00:22:53,360
of collateral damage

598
00:22:53,360 --> 00:22:54,480
that happens to people

599
00:22:54,480 --> 00:22:55,180
in the church

600
00:22:55,180 --> 00:22:56,400
when we run things that way.

601
00:22:56,400 --> 00:22:57,440
Paul says,

602
00:22:57,440 --> 00:22:58,580
you've got an urgent initiative,

603
00:22:58,580 --> 00:22:59,260
but it moves

604
00:22:59,260 --> 00:23:00,340
at the pace of relationship.

605
00:23:00,340 --> 00:23:01,340
It is rooted

606
00:23:01,340 --> 00:23:02,020
in humility,

607
00:23:02,020 --> 00:23:02,500
gentleness,

608
00:23:02,500 --> 00:23:03,040
patience,

609
00:23:03,040 --> 00:23:04,480
bearing with one another

610
00:23:04,480 --> 00:23:06,020
in love.

611
00:23:06,020 --> 00:23:06,940
Paul seems to be

612
00:23:06,940 --> 00:23:07,600
more concerned

613
00:23:07,600 --> 00:23:08,660
with how we go

614
00:23:08,660 --> 00:23:10,080
about this urgent initiative

615
00:23:10,080 --> 00:23:11,400
than the speed

616
00:23:11,400 --> 00:23:12,280
or extravagance

617
00:23:12,280 --> 00:23:13,840
in which we accomplish it.

618
00:23:14,640 --> 00:23:16,320
And if unity

619
00:23:16,320 --> 00:23:17,000
is the goal,

620
00:23:17,000 --> 00:23:18,000
it will require

621
00:23:18,000 --> 00:23:18,920
that we put on

622
00:23:18,920 --> 00:23:20,440
these attitudes.

623
00:23:20,440 --> 00:23:23,080
Unity is not

624
00:23:23,080 --> 00:23:24,000
formed

625
00:23:24,000 --> 00:23:25,240
without humility

626
00:23:25,240 --> 00:23:26,040
and gentleness

627
00:23:26,040 --> 00:23:26,720
and patience

628
00:23:26,720 --> 00:23:28,360
and enduring love.

629
00:23:28,360 --> 00:23:29,200
All of these

630
00:23:29,200 --> 00:23:29,700
are rooted

631
00:23:29,700 --> 00:23:31,320
in the character

632
00:23:31,320 --> 00:23:32,180
and example

633
00:23:32,180 --> 00:23:33,000
of Christ,

634
00:23:33,000 --> 00:23:34,160
which is what

635
00:23:34,160 --> 00:23:35,160
he goes on to say

636
00:23:35,160 --> 00:23:36,320
with the seven ones

637
00:23:36,320 --> 00:23:37,200
that this is all

638
00:23:37,200 --> 00:23:38,500
about what Jesus

639
00:23:38,500 --> 00:23:39,440
has done for us,

640
00:23:39,440 --> 00:23:40,620
that we are united

641
00:23:40,620 --> 00:23:41,560
around one Lord,

642
00:23:41,560 --> 00:23:42,500
one declaration

643
00:23:42,500 --> 00:23:43,100
of allegiance

644
00:23:43,100 --> 00:23:43,900
to that Lord,

645
00:23:43,900 --> 00:23:44,560
one baptism,

646
00:23:44,560 --> 00:23:45,680
one God and Father

647
00:23:45,680 --> 00:23:46,520
who is over all,

648
00:23:46,520 --> 00:23:47,020
through all,

649
00:23:47,020 --> 00:23:47,680
and in all.

650
00:23:47,680 --> 00:23:49,840
This is the only source

651
00:23:49,840 --> 00:23:50,660
of true unity

652
00:23:50,660 --> 00:23:52,240
for such a diverse

653
00:23:52,240 --> 00:23:53,040
group of people.

654
00:23:53,040 --> 00:23:54,460
We've talked about

655
00:23:54,460 --> 00:23:55,340
Jews and Gentiles,

656
00:23:55,340 --> 00:23:55,940
male, female,

657
00:23:55,940 --> 00:23:56,560
slaves, free.

658
00:23:56,560 --> 00:23:57,760
There's all these categories

659
00:23:57,760 --> 00:23:58,440
of people that have

660
00:23:58,440 --> 00:23:58,980
found themselves

661
00:23:58,980 --> 00:23:59,860
in one family

662
00:23:59,860 --> 00:24:01,660
and we only have

663
00:24:01,660 --> 00:24:02,300
true unity

664
00:24:02,300 --> 00:24:03,780
when we look

665
00:24:03,780 --> 00:24:04,600
to the example

666
00:24:04,600 --> 00:24:05,120
of Jesus,

667
00:24:05,120 --> 00:24:06,700
when we cultivate

668
00:24:06,700 --> 00:24:07,480
humility,

669
00:24:07,480 --> 00:24:08,020
gentleness,

670
00:24:08,020 --> 00:24:08,620
patience,

671
00:24:08,620 --> 00:24:11,220
and enduring love.

672
00:24:11,220 --> 00:24:12,620
And this is slow

673
00:24:12,620 --> 00:24:13,560
and so oftentimes

674
00:24:13,560 --> 00:24:14,600
we opt out

675
00:24:14,600 --> 00:24:17,560
because we live

676
00:24:17,560 --> 00:24:19,260
in a culture

677
00:24:19,260 --> 00:24:20,020
of microwaves.

678
00:24:20,020 --> 00:24:23,700
I literally

679
00:24:23,700 --> 00:24:25,000
just made egg bites

680
00:24:25,000 --> 00:24:25,460
in a minute

681
00:24:25,460 --> 00:24:26,220
and 30 seconds

682
00:24:26,220 --> 00:24:26,700
this morning.

683
00:24:27,580 --> 00:24:28,540
And so when I've

684
00:24:28,540 --> 00:24:29,140
been invited

685
00:24:29,140 --> 00:24:30,080
to participate

686
00:24:30,080 --> 00:24:31,400
in a new community

687
00:24:31,400 --> 00:24:33,120
of diverse believers

688
00:24:33,120 --> 00:24:36,880
from every language,

689
00:24:36,880 --> 00:24:37,540
tribe, nation,

690
00:24:37,540 --> 00:24:38,060
and tongue

691
00:24:38,060 --> 00:24:39,520
and we don't get along

692
00:24:39,520 --> 00:24:40,360
after week one,

693
00:24:40,360 --> 00:24:40,780
I'm like,

694
00:24:40,780 --> 00:24:42,720
I'll just start

695
00:24:42,720 --> 00:24:43,500
another community

696
00:24:43,500 --> 00:24:44,120
over here

697
00:24:44,120 --> 00:24:45,160
and I'll invite

698
00:24:45,160 --> 00:24:45,560
the people

699
00:24:45,560 --> 00:24:46,840
that think like I think,

700
00:24:46,840 --> 00:24:47,780
talk like I talk,

701
00:24:47,780 --> 00:24:48,760
act like I like,

702
00:24:48,760 --> 00:24:49,040
right?

703
00:24:49,040 --> 00:24:50,320
And it doesn't require

704
00:24:50,320 --> 00:24:51,000
as much humility,

705
00:24:51,000 --> 00:24:51,380
gentleness,

706
00:24:51,380 --> 00:24:53,020
but it's not maturing.

707
00:24:53,980 --> 00:24:55,700
It does not mature us

708
00:24:55,700 --> 00:24:57,180
if we do it that way.

709
00:24:57,180 --> 00:24:58,580
We've talked about this

710
00:24:58,580 --> 00:24:59,040
in the past,

711
00:24:59,040 --> 00:24:59,600
I don't have time

712
00:24:59,600 --> 00:25:00,480
to really unpack it.

713
00:25:00,480 --> 00:25:02,560
There's kind of two models

714
00:25:02,560 --> 00:25:05,060
of finding unity

715
00:25:05,060 --> 00:25:07,120
that some people

716
00:25:07,120 --> 00:25:07,660
have put together.

717
00:25:07,660 --> 00:25:07,960
It's called

718
00:25:07,960 --> 00:25:08,580
bounded set,

719
00:25:08,580 --> 00:25:09,140
centered set.

720
00:25:09,140 --> 00:25:10,040
Some of you remember this?

721
00:25:10,040 --> 00:25:10,320
Anybody?

722
00:25:10,320 --> 00:25:11,540
Somebody give me a...

723
00:25:11,540 --> 00:25:12,300
Thank you.

724
00:25:12,300 --> 00:25:12,480
All right,

725
00:25:12,480 --> 00:25:13,160
we got a few of them.

726
00:25:13,160 --> 00:25:14,860
Bounded set is this idea

727
00:25:14,860 --> 00:25:16,040
that I just draw a box

728
00:25:16,040 --> 00:25:17,000
around a group of people,

729
00:25:17,000 --> 00:25:18,140
I put hard, fast,

730
00:25:18,140 --> 00:25:19,600
legalistic requirements

731
00:25:19,600 --> 00:25:20,260
and lines

732
00:25:20,260 --> 00:25:21,360
and we all unite

733
00:25:21,360 --> 00:25:21,920
around the fact

734
00:25:21,920 --> 00:25:22,880
that we all agree

735
00:25:22,880 --> 00:25:24,440
about being in that box

736
00:25:24,440 --> 00:25:26,720
and oftentimes

737
00:25:26,720 --> 00:25:27,720
this is how the church

738
00:25:27,720 --> 00:25:28,620
has done unity.

739
00:25:28,620 --> 00:25:30,420
We have the longest

740
00:25:30,420 --> 00:25:31,240
belief statements

741
00:25:31,240 --> 00:25:32,380
that you could ever imagine.

742
00:25:32,380 --> 00:25:32,960
We all read

743
00:25:32,960 --> 00:25:34,180
from the same translation

744
00:25:34,180 --> 00:25:34,840
of the Bible.

745
00:25:34,840 --> 00:25:35,580
We all wear

746
00:25:35,580 --> 00:25:36,880
the same colored ties.

747
00:25:36,880 --> 00:25:37,700
We all like,

748
00:25:37,700 --> 00:25:38,760
it's all the same,

749
00:25:38,760 --> 00:25:39,060
right?

750
00:25:39,060 --> 00:25:41,520
And we're unified

751
00:25:41,520 --> 00:25:42,440
and I would say

752
00:25:42,440 --> 00:25:43,640
that is false unity.

753
00:25:43,640 --> 00:25:44,640
That is not real unity

754
00:25:44,640 --> 00:25:45,240
and that unity

755
00:25:45,240 --> 00:25:46,240
does not lead to maturity

756
00:25:46,240 --> 00:25:47,080
because you do not need

757
00:25:47,080 --> 00:25:47,500
to be humble,

758
00:25:47,500 --> 00:25:49,020
patient and enduring love

759
00:25:49,020 --> 00:25:50,320
when you are surrounded

760
00:25:50,320 --> 00:25:50,920
by people

761
00:25:50,920 --> 00:25:52,100
that are exactly like you.

762
00:25:52,100 --> 00:25:56,180
We opt out of maturity

763
00:25:56,180 --> 00:25:57,860
by pursuing false unity

764
00:25:57,860 --> 00:25:59,880
and I don't want to be

765
00:25:59,880 --> 00:26:00,720
a part of a church

766
00:26:00,720 --> 00:26:02,240
that has shallow unity.

767
00:26:02,240 --> 00:26:03,580
I want deep unity

768
00:26:03,580 --> 00:26:05,700
and the opposite side

769
00:26:05,700 --> 00:26:06,520
of that is centered set

770
00:26:06,520 --> 00:26:07,480
where we just put Jesus

771
00:26:07,480 --> 00:26:08,700
at the center of the circle

772
00:26:08,700 --> 00:26:10,840
and we keep our eyes on him

773
00:26:10,840 --> 00:26:11,800
and we all walk

774
00:26:11,800 --> 00:26:12,760
towards him together

775
00:26:12,760 --> 00:26:14,060
bearing with one another

776
00:26:14,060 --> 00:26:14,460
in love

777
00:26:14,460 --> 00:26:15,360
and we will disagree

778
00:26:15,360 --> 00:26:16,740
and we will have things

779
00:26:16,740 --> 00:26:17,800
that go wrong

780
00:26:17,800 --> 00:26:19,100
but at the end of the day

781
00:26:19,100 --> 00:26:21,740
it is maturing us

782
00:26:21,740 --> 00:26:22,560
into the image

783
00:26:22,560 --> 00:26:23,480
of Jesus.

784
00:26:23,480 --> 00:26:24,060
It's hard,

785
00:26:24,060 --> 00:26:24,620
it's deep

786
00:26:24,620 --> 00:26:25,440
but it's genuine

787
00:26:25,440 --> 00:26:26,700
and it cultivates maturity.

788
00:26:26,700 --> 00:26:28,360
Each of us

789
00:26:28,360 --> 00:26:29,660
as individual members

790
00:26:29,660 --> 00:26:30,420
of a local church

791
00:26:30,420 --> 00:26:31,500
are called to work

792
00:26:31,500 --> 00:26:33,500
towards genuine unity

793
00:26:33,500 --> 00:26:34,140
with humility,

794
00:26:34,140 --> 00:26:34,660
gentleness,

795
00:26:34,660 --> 00:26:36,260
patience and enduring love.

796
00:26:36,260 --> 00:26:38,120
With Jesus at the center

797
00:26:38,120 --> 00:26:39,060
it is slow

798
00:26:39,060 --> 00:26:40,240
and painful work

799
00:26:40,240 --> 00:26:41,960
but it does lead

800
00:26:41,960 --> 00:26:42,520
to maturity

801
00:26:42,520 --> 00:26:44,440
which is Paul's goal.

802
00:26:44,540 --> 00:26:45,800
you have an urgent initiative

803
00:26:45,800 --> 00:26:49,120
and that urgent initiative

804
00:26:49,120 --> 00:26:50,700
moves at the pace

805
00:26:50,700 --> 00:26:51,300
of relationship

806
00:26:51,300 --> 00:26:52,840
and produces maturity.

807
00:26:52,840 --> 00:26:53,480
He also says

808
00:26:53,480 --> 00:26:55,000
that it requires diversity.

809
00:26:55,000 --> 00:26:55,880
My second point here

810
00:26:55,880 --> 00:26:56,620
is that we walk

811
00:26:56,620 --> 00:26:58,020
with diversity.

812
00:26:58,020 --> 00:26:58,620
In verse 7

813
00:26:58,620 --> 00:26:58,940
he says,

814
00:26:58,940 --> 00:27:01,120
but to each one of us

815
00:27:01,120 --> 00:27:02,340
has been given

816
00:27:02,340 --> 00:27:05,340
as Christ apportioned it.

817
00:27:05,340 --> 00:27:07,900
Each one of us

818
00:27:07,900 --> 00:27:08,480
has grace

819
00:27:08,480 --> 00:27:09,420
has been given to us

820
00:27:09,420 --> 00:27:10,480
as Christ apportioned it.

821
00:27:11,120 --> 00:27:12,080
This is why it says

822
00:27:12,080 --> 00:27:13,380
when he ascended on high

823
00:27:13,380 --> 00:27:14,440
he took many captives

824
00:27:14,440 --> 00:27:15,440
and he gave gifts

825
00:27:15,440 --> 00:27:16,260
to his people.

826
00:27:16,260 --> 00:27:17,860
What does he ascended mean

827
00:27:17,860 --> 00:27:19,280
except that he also descended

828
00:27:19,280 --> 00:27:20,780
to the lower earthly regions.

829
00:27:20,780 --> 00:27:22,440
He who descended

830
00:27:22,440 --> 00:27:23,400
is the very one

831
00:27:23,400 --> 00:27:24,060
who ascended

832
00:27:24,060 --> 00:27:25,220
higher than all the heavens

833
00:27:25,220 --> 00:27:26,500
in order to fulfill

834
00:27:26,500 --> 00:27:27,620
the whole universe.

835
00:27:27,620 --> 00:27:28,920
So Christ himself

836
00:27:28,920 --> 00:27:30,380
gave the apostles,

837
00:27:30,380 --> 00:27:31,000
the prophets,

838
00:27:31,000 --> 00:27:31,640
the evangelists,

839
00:27:31,640 --> 00:27:32,100
the pastors

840
00:27:32,100 --> 00:27:32,920
and the teachers

841
00:27:32,920 --> 00:27:35,780
to equip his people

842
00:27:35,780 --> 00:27:37,120
for works of service

843
00:27:37,120 --> 00:27:38,860
so that the body of Christ

844
00:27:38,860 --> 00:27:39,980
may be built up

845
00:27:39,980 --> 00:27:42,040
until we all reach

846
00:27:42,040 --> 00:27:43,500
unity in the faith

847
00:27:43,500 --> 00:27:44,180
and knowledge

848
00:27:44,180 --> 00:27:45,620
in the Son of God

849
00:27:45,620 --> 00:27:46,920
and become mature

850
00:27:46,920 --> 00:27:48,480
attaining to the whole measure

851
00:27:48,480 --> 00:27:49,640
and fullness

852
00:27:49,640 --> 00:27:51,280
of Christ.

853
00:27:51,280 --> 00:27:52,940
Paul expounds

854
00:27:52,940 --> 00:27:53,940
on this call to unity

855
00:27:53,940 --> 00:27:54,760
saying that again

856
00:27:54,760 --> 00:27:56,460
true unity requires us

857
00:27:56,460 --> 00:27:57,540
to be in a group of people

